Debian 13 (trixie) for riscv64 on the Kakao SOC with kakao64

The card boots in one of two ways, by the device tree that
/sys/linux/boot.json on its FAT partition names (soc/docs/debian.md):

  kakao-busybox.dtb   a static busybox in this directory is init: a
                      root shell on the serial console and the first
                      terminal, and on the second, seconds after the
                      kernel. No password, no services.
  kakao.dtb           /sbin/init is init: Debian's own (systemd), once
                      it is installed. Minutes, on this CPU.

What is here for the first:

  /opt/kakao/busybox  init (its table: /etc/inittab) and the tools the
                      base system lacks: reboot, poweroff, ip, ping, vi,
                      ... as links in /usr/local/sbin
  /opt/kakao/rcS      mounts, the host name, DHCP on eth0, the time by NTP

The clock starts at 1970 when there is no network: apt refuses the
archive then. Set it:    date -s "2026-11-25 10:00"

To install Debian's init, with a cable plugged in:

  /opt/kakao/install-systemd

Its steps are in it, to do by hand if it stops. Nothing of the busybox
way is removed by it: name kakao-busybox.dtb in boot.json again (on a
PC, or here: mount /dev/vda1 /mnt) and the card boots as before.
